From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolzen <funer@gmx.at>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cec, user: Stop on the end of a D-Bus stream instead of
 spinning

The cecd listener drains the ObjectManager signals it does not use with
`_ = stream.next() => ()`, and the signal relay forwards
MaxChargeLevelChanged with `_ = stream.next()`. `_` also matches the
`None` a stream returns once its connection is closed, and the stream then
returns `None` again at once: the select runs that branch forever. The
future never returns Pending, so the task never yields: one tokio worker
stays at 100 % CPU, and the task's cancellation is never polled, so the
daemon no longer exits on SIGTERM either (it waits for that task).

This happens to the session half whenever its session bus goes away while
it keeps running, as on systems without systemd --user, where each login
has its own session bus: after every switch between game mode and the
desktop, the old session's steamos-manager kept a core busy and survived
the logout's SIGTERM, and the fan stayed loud.

The end of the stream now ends the service with an error, as a closed
connection elsewhere in the daemon does, and the daemon shuts down.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/steamos-manager/src/cec.rs
+++ b/steamos-manager/src/cec.rs
@@ -481,7 +481,13 @@
                             None
                         };
                     },
-                    _ = device_added.next() => (), // Drain these ever if we're not using them
+                    // Drain these even if we're not using them. The stream
+                    // only ends when the connection to cecd's bus is gone;
+                    // matching that end with `_` would run this branch again
+                    // at once, forever, without ever yielding.
+                    signal = device_added.next() => if signal.is_none() {
+                        bail!("Connection to cecd closed");
+                    },
                 };
             } else {
                 select! {
@@ -500,7 +506,10 @@
                             None
                         };
                     },
-                    _ = device_removed.next() => (), // Drain these even if we're not using them
+                    // Drain these even if we're not using them (see above)
+                    signal = device_removed.next() => if signal.is_none() {
+                        bail!("Connection to cecd closed");
+                    },
                 };
             }
         }
--- a/steamos-manager/src/manager/user.rs
+++ b/steamos-manager/src/manager/user.rs
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
  */
 
-use anyhow::{Error, Result};
+use anyhow::{Error, Result, bail};
 use async_trait::async_trait;
 use cecd_proxy::Config1Proxy;
 use serde::Deserialize;
@@ -1653,7 +1653,12 @@
 
         loop {
             select! {
-                _ = max_charge_level_changed.next() => {
+                signal = max_charge_level_changed.next() => {
+                    // The stream only ends with the system bus connection;
+                    // `_` would match that end over and over (busy loop).
+                    if signal.is_none() {
+                        bail!("Connection to the system bus closed");
+                    }
                     if let Some(battery_charge_limit1) = battery_charge_limit1.as_mut() {
                         battery_charge_limit1.signal_emitter().max_charge_level_changed().await?;
                     }
